% -e over the shapes of an existence check.  A positive literal whose
% columns not bound before it hold `_` or a variable its rule mentions
% nowhere else binds nothing the rule reads, and is a test of whether some
% tuple agrees with its bound columns: keyed through the index on them,
% printed with its key, when some are bound, and asking whether the
% relation is empty when none is.  A named variable mentioned once, _To,
% is planned and printed as `_`, as the rule line shows the name it was
% given.  In the recursive rule the literal holding `_` is checked through
% the view its place in each delta variant gives it: the delta, or the
% tuples older than it.  The query streams, since its check lets each
% binding of X through once.  The program is answered without the Magic
% rewrite, so that every rule's plan is shown.

edge(a, b).
edge(b, c).
edge(c, d).
edge(c, e).
node(a).
node(b).
node(c).

leaves(X) :- node(X), edge(X, _).
named(X) :- node(X), edge(X, _To).
nonempty(X) :- node(X), edge(_, _).

path(X, Y) :- edge(X, Y).
path(X, Z) :- path(Z, _), path(X, Y), edge(Y, Z).

node(X), edge(_, X)?
